Commit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Nov 3 07:07:35 2026 +0700

    test(yang.clojure): D2 revise — the forged-vector regression exercises the packet dispatch
    
    The previous regression was vacuous: it applied the extracted entry
    through source-level lowering, and admission refused the raw closure
    before the entry ever executed — so it passed against the broken
    implementation too. The regression now projects the descriptor into a
    compiled program via postwalk, applies the extracted entry to forged
    vectors ([42], [nil [42]], [], [a b c d]) inside that program on both
    evaluators, and asserts the body's marker value never occurs (10
    assertions green). The compiler's P1 fix — the vector alternate returns
    an explicit refusal instead of applying the private body — is
    unchanged; the witness callable? guard and the native-assoc
    implementation of dsg__assoc are restored. Focused gate: counts
    {pass 102, recorded-upstream-failure 2, recorded-deviation 2, blocked
    0}; exactly the by-design assertion failing; kondo 0/0.

