{"role":"assistant","content":"## Verdict: **REJECT — the replacement regression is still vacuous**\n\nThe new test has four independent problems at `test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1360-1389`:\n\n1. **The projected descriptor is never used.**  \n   The postwalk replaces `(u/v 'descriptor)`, but the compiled program contains no `descriptor` or `dsc` variable. It still defines and calls `target`. The manually constructed `descriptor` is therefore irrelevant.\n\n2. **Both lanes are the walker.**  \n   `run` ignores `lane`; both `walker` and `semantic` execute:\n\n   ```clojure\n   (tu/create-vm ...)\n   (tu/queue-ast! ...)\n   ```\n\n   Neither calls `semantic-run` or `semantic/create-vm`.\n\n3. **The source-level admission refusal remains.**  \n   The program still contains:\n\n   ```clojure\n   (let [raw (yang.call/entry target)]\n     (raw 'forged))\n   ```\n\n   Thus admission refuses the raw closure before packet dispatch, exactly as in the previous version.\n\n4. **The assertion cannot detect body entry.**  \n   `result` is either `[:completed payload]` or `[:error message]`. Comparing that entire value with `:private-body-entered` is always true, including when the payload is `[:yin.k/ok :private-body-entered]`. `status` is destructured but never asserted.\n\nConsequently, the test would also pass against the original body-applying defect.\n\n### Required correction\n\nReplace the final call with an actual **direct UAST application** of the extracted entry, then use the existing helpers:\n\n```clojure\n(doseq [run [walker-run semantic-run]]\n  (let [result (first (run call-ast))]\n    (is (= :yin.k/error (first result)))\n    (is (not= [:yin.k/ok :private-body-entered] result))))\n```\n\nThe direct UAST must apply the entry itself—not pass it through `compile-guest-call`. Asserting a side-effect log remains the stronger non-entry proof.\n\n### Other items\n\nThe production refusal and helper restorations remain correct. The discharge counts are acceptable, but exact `check-accepted` walker and semantic counts are still unreported; “well under” does not satisfy that outstanding requirement.\n\nNo landing approval until the regression genuinely reaches packet dispatch on both evaluators and fails against the old defective alternate."}
